.TH LIBRDP 7 "2026-07-12" "librdp 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
librdp \- C client library for RDP viewers and integration tools
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librdp
is a C client library for building RDP viewers and integration tools on Unix-like systems. The library exposes opaque settings, session, event, surface, input, clipboard, audio, video, and channel APIs.
.P
The core library is platform-neutral. Host windowing, media, device, authenticator, and clipboard integration belong to applications or viewer backends.
.SH OBJECTS
.TP
.B librdp_settings
Configuration object for target, credentials, security mode, TLS policy, gateway transport, desktop size, feature flags, and redirected devices. Sessions clone settings during construction.
.TP
.B librdp_session
Client session object owning transport, protocol, channel, cache, graphics, and active surface state.
.TP
.B librdp_surface
Framebuffer surface object exposing BGRA pixel data to viewers.
.TP
.B librdp_event
Callback-delivered event object. Payloads are borrowed and valid only until the callback returns.
.TP
.B librdp_workspace
Workspace feed object owning copied feed configuration and parsed published resources.
.SH LIFECYCLE
A typical application allocates settings, configures them, creates a session, registers an event callback, connects, repeatedly calls
.BR librdp_session_run_once (),
presents surface updates, sends input or feature responses, disconnects, and frees objects.
.SH THREADING
Objects are not internally synchronized. Applications must serialize calls operating on the same settings, session, or surface object unless they provide external locking.
.SH SECURITY
Credentials and sensitive user data must not be logged. Trace is disabled by default and protocol hexdumps are bounded. Applications own user consent for clipboard, audio, camera, filesystem, smartcard, USB, WebAuthn, printer, and other host resources.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I include/librdp/*.h
Public headers.
.TP
.I docs/api-reference.md
Header-oriented API map.
.TP
.I docs/programmers-reference.md
Application integration manual.
.TP
.I docs/lifecycle.md
Application-visible sequencing for sessions, graphics, input, channels, devices, and teardown.
.TP
.I docs/backend-guide.md
Host backend contracts for media, devices, clipboard, printers, and authenticators.
.TP
.I docs/generated-api.md
Entry point for generated per-symbol API documentation.
